# The loopback certificate: 140 words out through the transmitter's own
# `sona` and back through the receiver, in one process, with no WAV and no
# pipe. One byte a word, 0 when the seventeen bytes came back equal;
# expected.out is 140 zero bytes, so a single wrong word names itself by its
# offset (word 0 is the zero word, words 1..136 have wire bit i = word - 1
# set, words 137..139 are the three frames vendor/hydramodem-tx/ holds WAVs
# for).
#
# It reads nothing: the binary audits to `write` and `exit_group` (plus the
# `read` the `ambitus` gate carries), where receptio_loopback/'s also reads.
#
# This is the test the four blind spots of docs/design/receptor.md section 6
# are stated against, and the one that takes every edge of D8's trellis: 140
# words x 158 steps, with the zero word's tail and 136 one-hot words between
# them.
#
# Cost: 1.2 s measured at the commit that added it -- 140 decodes of 19,008
# samples each, acquisition scan included -- against the harness's 20-second
# limit. If a future change pushes it past that, the directory splits in two
# rather than the certificate shrinking.
TEST: expect-exit=0 sources=examples/hydramodem/quantum.exsc,examples/hydramodem/modulator.exsc,examples/hydramodem/receptor.exsc,examples/hydramodem/circuitus.exsc
